x4591 call open x4590 15
x4592 write x4591 2
x4593 text "Is the compiler deterministic?"
x4594 puts x4592 x4593
x4595 call close x4594 
x4596 call open x4595 2
x4597 write x4596 2
x4598 text "Yes. No model is involved in compilation. Same source, same bytes, on every target, with content-addressed caching keyed by the semantic revision of each function."
x4599 puts x4597 x4598
x4600 call close x4599 
x4601 call close x4600 
x4602 call open x4601 5
x4603 write x4602 4
x4604 write x4603 2
x4605 text "card reveal"
x4606 puts x4604 x4605
x4607 call open x4606 15
x4608 write x4607 2
x4609 text "How is correctness checked?"
x4610 puts x4608 x4609
x4611 call close x4610 
x4612 call open x4611 2
x4613 write x4612 2
x4614 text "A BigInt oracle runs 5262 generated cases through every backend, the optimizer is proved equivalent to the source with Z3 on all 48 corpus functions, hardware is simulated in Icarus and synthesized in Yosys, and hand-written C, Rust, JavaScript and Python are the benchmark baselines."
x4615 puts x4613 x4614
x4616 call close x4615 
x4617 call close x4616 
x4618 call close x4617 
x4619 call open x4618 15
x4620 write x4619 4
x4621 write x4620 2
x4622 text "head"
x4623 puts x4621 x4622
x4624 write x4623 2
x4625 text "What A0 does not do yet"
x4626 puts x4624 x4625
x4627 call close x4626 
x4628 call open x4627 5
x4629 write x4628 4
x4630 write x4629 2
x4631 text "limits"
x4632 puts x4630 x4631
x4633 call open x4632 2
x4634 write x4633 2
x4635 text "No floating point, no strings beyond byte arrays, no heap or dynamic sizes (arrays are fixed-length values), no recursion, no exceptions. Whole-task token cost is higher than TypeScript because a new language must ship its primer on every call. The direct native backend covers AArch64 today; x86-64, 32-bit ARM, RISC-V, and AVR are next, and until each passes the corpus it is not listed as supported."
x4636 puts x4634 x4635
x4637 call close x4636 
x4638 call close x4637 
x4639 call open x4638 15
x4640 write x4639 4
x4641 write x4640 2
x4642 text "head"
